# CRA's built-in build-time ESLint (driven by the legacy `eslintConfig` block that used
# to live in package.json) resolves `eslint-config-react-app` from the project root.
# Adding the independent `npm run lint` gate (eslint.config.js — FSD boundaries, react-hooks)
# pulled in eslint@9 and friends as top-level devDependencies, and npm's hoisting no longer
# keeps `eslint-config-react-app` resolvable at the root as a side effect — any future
# devDependency change can shift it again. Rather than fight hoisting churn to keep two
# separate, unequal lint setups alive, CRA's weaker internal one is disabled; `npm run lint`
# is the single source of truth now. (Moot again once Stage 2 replaces CRA with Vite.)
DISABLE_ESLINT_PLUGIN=true
